      "passage_id": "statement.body",
      "label": "Recorded statement of Dana Whitfield",
      "text": "[00:00:12] ADJUSTER: Can you take me through what happened on the fourteenth?\n[00:00:18] MS WHITFIELD: I'd been at my sister's on Willow Street. I left there and I was heading north, back towards the junction.\n[00:00:31] ADJUSTER: And roughly what speed were you doing?\n[00:00:34] MS WHITFIELD: Twenty, twenty-five. It is a narrow road, you cannot do much more.\n[00:00:41] ADJUSTER: So you were stopped at the light when the other vehicle hit you, is that right?\n[00:00:47] MS WHITFIELD: No, I was still moving. I had not got to the lights yet.\n[00:00:53] ADJUSTER: What time would this have been?\n[00:00:56] MS WHITFIELD: That evening, after I had my tea. I could not tell you exactly.\n[00:01:04] ADJUSTER: And you reported it to us on the twentieth?\n[00:01:08] MS WHITFIELD: That is right. I wanted to see if the other driver would sort it first.",
